--TEST--
`query` answers a `Core\Db\Rows`, so a result set is a type of its own rather than the array `fetchAll` hands back — `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members` and `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::query
// `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members` makes `Core\Db\Connection::query` the buffered member — every
// row is read before it answers, and the connection is free again — and what
// it answers with is a `Db\Rows` rather than an array. The difference is § 6's:
// a `Rows` knows the columns the server described, so its rows carry typed
// readers that answer `?T`, where an array element is whatever the driver
// happened to make of it and `$row["id"] == 1` silently fails.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

array<mixed> $wrong = $db->query("select 1", []);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `array<mixed>`, found `Core\Db\Rows<Core\Db\Row>`
   --> case.nvs:11:23
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
